WEBVTT

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.650
The onboard staff are all missing.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.430
We've located seven of eighty-two passengers.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.050
Four show signs of Apathy Syndrome.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.660
So only three made it out safely.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.760
I'm not sure about that.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.430
And by that?

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.470
As we confirmed their identities,
their claims and the facts don't add up.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.700
...What do you mean?

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.060
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.860
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.600
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.000
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.180
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.210
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.580
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.620
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.290
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.130
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:42.060
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to the voices before it collapses

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:47.940
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.680
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:01:53.680 --> 00:02:05.290
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.090
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:14.900
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.660
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.920
Megumi-san, you were amazing!

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.150
Thanks for coming, everyone.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.400
It's kinda sad this is your last performance.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.330
There's an official show coming up, right?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.740
It would be a bother if us seniors
stuck around for too long.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.170
The show in the fall is for the underclassmen. Plus...

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.310
I think today's show was the
best performance I've done.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.910
You look like you got over
something while we were in Yatsuo.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.510
Huh? Oh...

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:08.840
Yeah.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:16.320
Megumi-san, can you teach
me how to dance sometime?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.490
Huh? I didn't know you were interested in dancing.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.500
Yeah, just a little...

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.670
Then once you're in 10th grade,
you should join the club.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.540
I know it's called the "club,"
but we're still not official.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.680
Will you join them and make it happen?

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.480
But Jun, they're all girls.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.680
It might motivate other
boys to join if Jun-kun does.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:46.820
Yeah, don't ruin this, Takuro.
You're terrible at dancing, anyway.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:47.890
Shut up!

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:57.630
Them?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.430
I heard there are more and more lately.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.200
They're being called the "Vanishing Wills."

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.690
Vanishing?

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.970
You know the news about people
disappearing at Toyama Bay every so often?

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:17.650
Those who've lost their will to live go to
the shore and wait to get taken away.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.680
It's kinda scary.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.460
It's like everyone is falling into apathy.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.360
It... reminds me of ten years ago.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.940
You were still living here then, right?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.400
Huh? Yeah...

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.000
But I... don't remember much about that day.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.650
Sorry for bringing it up...

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.740
Huh? No, I mean, seriously...

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.940
Takuro?

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:14.870
What's wrong?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:16.640
Hey.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.440
U-umm... What?

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:20.910
It's me.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.710
Did you forget? It's Takuro. I'm your...

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.860
Um, my name is Mizutani, and...

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.390
H-hey, Takuro!?

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.060
Hey, what's wrong!?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.600
Sorry... It's nothing. I got the wrong person.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.480
...Um, we're sorry.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.550
Sorry.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.910
Hey, Takuro!?

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.720
How did it go?

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.650
You can't tell by looking at him,

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:07.500
but his personality and consciousness have
been replaced by none other than that

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.270
of temporary chief Kubo's missing
brother-in-law, Sema Yuko-san's husband.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.140
However, his body is of a
completely different person.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.130
According to the family of Asano Takuma-san,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:21.340
the submarine crewman who disappeared half
a year ago during the ocean development...

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.800
It was definitely his body.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.680
Over here, too.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:32.050
Nagai from Hiiragi Pharmaceutical, who
showed a small sign of Apathy Syndrome,

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.360
was found in Uotsu and
taken into custody yesterday.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.050
He turned into a different
person during the interrogation.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.620
We thought he was acting at first, but...

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.330
Just like the remaining ferryboat passengers...

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.400
Did you get to ask anything
while Nagai was himself?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.340
Nothing major.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.540
But the means of communication between him and
the Marebito was through an illegal drug forum.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:01.220
His act of betrayal to Hiiragi came from a
disagreement about how everything was handled,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.550
and then jumping onto the anti-president
bandwagon against Hiiragi.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.410
Apparently, he was trying to raise
funds to negotiate with others.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:15.960
To be safe, I will have him confirm the culprits
in the kidnapping case half a year ago.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:22.760
Even if they were instigated by him, it will be
impossible to prove in his current state, however...

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.610
I don't intend to go back.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.970
What was the point of getting out of the
group to continue with the research?

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.840
We're just repeating the same mistake.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:44.350
There are inevitable sacrifices,
but many are unnecessary!

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.390
Do not forget you're still human.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.840
Onii...oniichan.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:02.370
I went and ventilated the house.
It's all locked up, too.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.870
Oh, thanks!

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.000
A Whale's Feather?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.480
Yeah, I've been thinking about it lately.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.420
The feathers were there... at the shoreline.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.620
Yeah.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.720
That was Takuro-san's dad.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:17.420
What?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:23.260
The person who left Takuro-san
when he was little...

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.370
You sense all those things, huh?

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:40.170
Huh?

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:41.870
Doesn't it get tough for you?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:49.920
It sounds hard to keep everything
to yourself when you know so much.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:57.330
I'm glad you told me about Takuro.
He was acting strange, even for him.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.330
Otherwise, I would've asked him about it later.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:07.200
Oniichan, right now...

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:17.320
Ayane-chan...

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.620
The Whale is scared.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.490
Your dad?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.800
Yeah.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.430
That man earlier?

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.500
He was a good-for-nothing.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.270
For New Customers Only
Cut
Color
Perm
Straightening

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:47.750
When I was five, I was watching
the Cycloid V's live show...

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:50.150
Cycloid V?

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:53.820
It's an effect-heavy hero story from long ago.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:57.160
The re-runs became popular when we were little.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.890
I've seen it a few times before.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.160
So, since then...

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:06.890
Yeah... My mom couldn't get over him for a
while, but as soon as she got a new boyfriend...

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.940
Sorry, you wouldn't wanna hear something like this.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:11.870
It's fine.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:16.680
If you wanna talk about it, we'll listen anytime.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.110
Yup. And if you don't wanna, that's fine, too.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:20.880
Right?

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:27.720
Anyway, I didn't think he would act like that.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.820
I shouldn't have stopped him.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.220
By the way, your dad seemed rather young.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.730
Oh... Now that you mention it...

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:39.790
Takuro?

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:41.700
Is that you, Takuro?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.910
Um, yes, I'm Sakakiba Takuro.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.470
I knew it! It's me, Takuro!

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:50.330
Y-you're?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.800
Your dad.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.950
You've grown so much.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:01.220
But that fried-noodle-ish hair of yours...

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.760
H-hey, wait a sec, lady! You're joking.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.290
Um, let's go.

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.450
O-okay.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.230
Takuro!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.390
I wanted you-

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:14.890
About Cycloid V-

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.530
The Whale is ill.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:46.170
That day... this city and the
sea connected with the Whale.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.800
The Whale can feel them.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:52.010
The unbelievable distortion, created
through force by people, and the pain...

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.570
I was one of them, too.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.370
The Whale is the Sea of Psyche.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:02.780
It lies quietly and deeply,
down in everyone and everything.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.010
This is the scab.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.420
The Whale's screaming.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.290
...Is my brother with you?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.910
He's with the Whale.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.940
He doesn't want anything...
He wishes for everything to disappear.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:41.980
The scab?

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.920
The Whale's... screaming?

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.890
What's up, Jun?

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.270
Oniichan, um...

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.200
Excuse me.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.600
Does Sakakiba Takuro attend this academy?

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.340
Takuro is my roommate in the dorms.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.680
Really? I'm glad.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:08.750
I'm Takuro's...

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.710
Nevermind... Can you give this to him?

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.490
The dorms are nearby.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:17.580
Isn't he at work now?

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:18.990
Oh, you're right.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:23.520
I would just confuse him. Plus, I can't
possibly show my face to him now.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:30.030
But especially because of that,
this gave me the courage...

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.840
U-um...

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.800
But...

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.730
It looks like I don't have much time.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.290
...Can't be.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.960
See ya.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.720
I'll walk you out.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.930
Hey, welcome back.

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:58.960
I'm back!

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:01.840
What's that, Kanzato-kun?

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.700
It's from some lady I've never seen before.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.170
Is it a gift?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.370
No, she wanted me to give it to Takuro.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:15.620
I didn't understand what she was
talking about, but she seemed serious.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:21.290
Was that lady tall and pretty?

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.050
Was she wearing a pink jacket?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.150
Yeah, something like that.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:31.020
She might actually be Takuro-kun's father.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:39.000
Something similar to what happened
by Toyama Bay is happening in the city.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:45.400
The missing people are returning... but
their body and psyche aren't matching up.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.680
We've confirmed cases

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:51.950
where Apathy Syndrome patients possess
memories and personalities of those missing.

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:53.720
What does that?

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.480
This is beyond belief.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.220
Our common understanding is the
body and psyche are indivisible.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:04.730
Some kind of distortion is occurring,
somewhere deep and unseen to us.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:06.130
That is...

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.900
an abnormal distortion.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:13.230
It's like a calm sea starting to grow hazardous.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:18.740
But I have no idea why it's
happening here or at Toyama Bay.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.080
What's wrong?

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.180
Oh, no, nothing.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.050
You get lost in thought too, huh?

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.220
Sometimes, but not as often as you.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.030
I don't know what's been bothering you,

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:43.300
but try to be careful when you're
walking around or ringing up customers.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:44.840
Takuro!

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.900
Hey, what's up, guys?

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:50.440
This...

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:52.780
What is it?

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:55.580
I got it from someone claiming to be your dad.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.680
You know, that lady from earlier today.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.960
Sakakiba-kun, is that?

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.020
It's Cycloid V, right?

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.970
Th-that's one of the original versions... Cool!

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:15.700
Takuro... That lady might actually be your dad.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:16.900
I don't really know, but...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.070
She might really be.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.630
I keep thinking that.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:26.350
I got into it after he made
me watch the rental videos.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:30.410
Every time my mom was fed up with it,
he would claim that Cycloid V is "deep."

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.240
How stupid.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.910
Who cares about such an idiot dad?

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.130
Takuro...

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.990
I'm sure he'll be back if he needs something.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:42.350
Time is running out.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.560
That's what she was saying.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.030
What the hell?

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:54.870
I don't know... but I think she meant,
like, she can't stay for too long.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:41.520
Takuro... how did you?

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.590
It's not fair.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.790
I can't beat you up when you look like that.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.800
How have you been since then?

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.110
Right here...

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.650
I left you.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.740
How could you ask that?

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:17.380
I lived with Grandma.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.960
She passed away during the
string of accidents back then.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:24.300
Uncle's family moved here.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.200
They let me stay with them until
I finished middle school, but...

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.860
Were they cold to you?

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.830
At home and school? All because of me...

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.310
Let's not.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:42.070
Since I changed my hair, punks stayed away.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.810
Enough about me.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:51.150
Mom wanted to be with you.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.550
No matter how hard it would've been.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:59.290
The one who made her that way was...

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:12.000
You took on everything by
yourself and disappeared.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:16.580
The debt wasn't even yours to repay.

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:25.350
I'm sorry.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.760
Oh! Right...

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.740
You know...

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.970
You set an example for me not to follow.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.910
I'll never make the love of my life cry.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.740
I'll never betray the people who believe in me.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.680
I see... That's good.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.350
It's time to say goodbye, Takuro.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.160
Dad?

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:06.190
I'm glad we got to see each other, in the end.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.530
Thank you, Takuro...

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.170
Take this!

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.700
You're the one who likes this!

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.500
I'm not that...

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:22.540
Cycloid V is deep, Takuro.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:52.470
How is it deep?

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.520
Should we watch it?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.850
Wanna have a little get-together?

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.450
You guys can use my room.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.450
I wanna see, too.

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.460
Me, too!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.660
Then, should we stop by the-

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.630
Yeah, the rental shop, right?

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.650
No... we can go straight back.

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.790
I have the DVDs.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:58.150
Itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
